<title>USA: Texas natgas in storage estimated at 103.58 bcf.</title>
<headline>Texas natgas in storage estimated at 103.58 bcf.</headline>
<dateline>AUSTIN, Texas 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Natural gas in storage in February was estimated at 103.58 billion cubic feet (bcf), the Texas Railroad Commission said on Friday.</p>
<p>Natural gas in storage in January was pegged at 124.41 bcf, down from 154.16 bcf in January 1996, the state agency regulating oil and gas exploration and production in Texas said.</p>
<p>The commission set March allowable production from prorated fields in the state at 71.78 bcf, down 5.19 bcf from actual production of 76.97 bcf in March 1996.</p>
<p>-- Houston Bureau ((713 210-8508))</p>
